{
  "name": "Scenario 3 | Google Sheets polling to email automation (Via Google forms/sheets)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "Google sheets to Email automations\nConnect your Google Form to a linked Google Sheet (Form responses go straight into Sheet rows natively by Google).\nIn n8n, instead of a Webhook node, you use the Google Sheets Trigger node.\nHow it works:\nIf your laptop is offline for 5 hours and 20 people submit the form, all 20 rows sit safely inside the Google Sheet.\nThe moment you turn Docker back on, n8n wakes up, looks at the Google Sheet, sees 20 new rows it hasn't processed yet, and processes all 20 of them in a row!\nAnalogy: This is a Mailbox. Even if you are away on vacation, letters pile up in the mailbox, and you read them all when you get home",
        "height": 208,
        "width": 1088,
        "color": 5
      },
